# Class -> Rust path glob (relative to crates/fr-settings/src) map for scripts/audit-port.sh's
# per-class matching (Plan 3 Task 1 obligation, reused here per plan Task 1). Blank lines and
# lines starting with `#` are ignored. Append one line per class as later Plan 4 tasks port it; do
# not remove a class's line once a task starts porting it, or the audit falls back to a crate-wide
# (weaker) check for it. A class whose Rust home spans more than one file gets one map line per
# file — not one line with several space-separated globs, which the reader (`read -r cls path`)
# would only keep the first token of.
RouterSettings              router_settings.rs
RouterSettings              board_optimizations.rs
RouterSettings              copy_fields.rs
LayerSettings               layer_settings.rs
ScoringSettings             scoring_settings.rs
OptimizerSettings           optimizer_settings.rs
FanoutSettings              fanout_settings.rs
DesignRulesCheckerSettings  drc_settings.rs
DebugSettings               drc_settings.rs
SettingsSource              merger.rs
SettingsMerger              merger.rs
ReflectionUtil              copy_fields.rs
ReflectionUtil              field_path.rs
DefaultSettings             sources/default_settings.rs
DsnFileSettings             sources/dsn_file.rs
RulesFileSettings           sources/rules_file.rs
SesFileSettings             sources/ses_file.rs
ApiSettings                 sources/api.rs
EnvironmentVariablesSource  sources/env.rs
CliSettings                 sources/cli.rs
GlobalSettings              sources/cli.rs
JsonFileSettings            sources/json_file.rs
GuiSettingsSource           lib.rs
# Task 10: the Gson configuration `RouterSettings`'s JSON in/out reproduces. Task 11 added
# `util/gson` as a fourth audit invocation (see `crates/fr-settings/README.md`), so every class in
# that package is mapped here. `RouterSettingsTypeAdapterFactory` spans three files: the
# `// not ported:` markers for its `create`/`read` methods are in `lib.rs`'s roster, and its
# `write` half — Plan 5 Task 1 moved the actual `JavaNumberFormatter` (and `GsonProvider.GSON`'s
# configuration of it) down into `fr-dsn::format::json` so `fr-drc` can reuse it without depending
# on this crate (ruling 7) — is `../../fr-dsn/src/format/json.rs`. The three adapters below carry
# no `RouterSettings` type at all and are roster-only.
GsonProvider                json.rs
GsonProvider                ../../fr-dsn/src/format/json.rs
RouterSettingsTypeAdapterFactory lib.rs
RouterSettingsTypeAdapterFactory ../../fr-dsn/src/format/json.rs
InstantTypeAdapter          lib.rs
PathTypeAdapter             lib.rs
ByteArrayToBase64TypeAdapter lib.rs
